# Normalize line endings for all text files; force LF in the working tree too,
# so a Windows checkout does not flag LF files as modified.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must always use LF (prevents CRLF issues on Windows)
*.sh text eol=lf

# Committed Vite build output is opaque bytes: no line-ending normalization
# (any mangling on checkout/commit would false-fail the byte-exact freshness
# gate, scripts/check-webui-dist.sh) and no textual diffs of the minified
# bundles ("Binary files differ" keeps PR diffs and the gate's failure output
# readable).
playground/dist/** -text -diff
# ...except index.html: 14 lines of readable HTML whose hashed-bundle <script>/
# <link> swap is the most informative line in a UI-bump PR. Keep -text (no
# normalization, same as the bundles) but restore textual diffs.
playground/dist/index.html -text diff
